1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
You book a flight through a travel agent.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Confirmation in your inbox. You're packed. You're headed to the airport.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:12,000
But the airline sent a delay notice an hour ago.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:17,000
You walk into the terminal. The board shows your flight — delayed. And you had no idea.

5
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,000
This happened in Abuja on May 27th, 2026.

6
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Because travel agents had put their own contact details in the booking record.

7
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:30,000
This is PAX.

8
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,000
It checks whether the airline's booking record actually contains your own contact details.

9
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:40,000
Not just an email somewhere. Your email. Your phone. Attached to you.

10
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:45,000
You enter and verify your own email and phone.

11
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:50,000
PAX reads CTCE for email, CTCM for mobile, CTCR when a passenger declines.

12
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Here's what it finds.

13
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:00,000
This booking — two passengers. One passenger's phone number got attached to the other.

14
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Also flagged.

15
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:10,000
Before anything is written, you give explicit consent.

16
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:15,000
You review the proposed change. You approve it.

17
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:20,000
PAX reloads the booking in a completely fresh read.

18
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:25,000
Only then does it mark you verified.

19
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Before and after. Timestamps. Masked contacts. Proof.

20
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:35,000
But what if the system lies?

21
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:40,000
That's the Drey moment.

22
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:45,000
Kane CLI opens a real browser. Reloads the booking.

23
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:50,000
And finds — nothing was saved. The green toast was a lie.

24
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:55,000
The agent reads Kane's failure evidence. Fixes the persistence path.

25
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Reruns Kane. And this time — the contact is really there.

26
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Here's what I'll tell you straight.

27
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:10,000
The demo runs on a Carrier Sandbox — not a live airline.

28
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:15,000
PAX doesn't guarantee your airline will send you a text.

29
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:20,000
It proves the record contains your contact — at the time of verification.

30
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,000
Most travel tools tell you about your flight.

31
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:30,000
PAX asks whether the airline can reach you.

32
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:35,000
Try it. Clone the repo. Seed the sandbox. Run the audit.

33
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,000
PAX. Because the airline should be able to reach the person who bought the ticket.
